# Line endings: normalise everything to LF in the repository *and* on checkout.
#
# `text=auto` alone only normalises what gets stored; each checkout then gets its
# native ending, so a Windows clone produces CRLF. That breaks shell scripts,
# Dockerfiles and Makefiles when the same tree is later used in Linux or WSL.
# Pinning eol=lf also overrides the reviewer's core.autocrlf, so every machine
# gets byte-identical working trees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF, because some shells require it there.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never diff, merge or convert binary content.
*.db     binary
*.db-shm binary
*.db-wal binary
*.sqlite binary
*.ico    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
